<title>USA: Golden Pharmaceuticals sells I-123 assets.</title>
<headline>Golden Pharmaceuticals sells I-123 assets.</headline>
<dateline>GOLDEN, Colo. 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Golden Pharmaceuticals Inc said Friday it sold the assets related to its Iodine-123 business to Syncor Pharmaceuticals Inc, a wholly owned subsidiary of Syncor International Corp.</p>
<p>The company said the new drug application for I-123 capsules, the building that contains the manufacturing plant for the capsules and the equipment related to the I-123 business were all included in the sale.</p>
<p>The company also said Robert Bogle was appointed chief operating officer of its Quality Care Pharmaceuticals Inc division.</p>
